===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|moder in lawe}}; equivalent to {{af|en|mother|-in-law}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmʌ.ðəɹ.ɪnˌlɔː/|a=UK,US}} ({{enPR|mŭˈ -''th''ər-ĭn-lôˌ}})
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmʌ.ðəɹ.ɪnˌlɑː/|a=cot-caught}} ({{enPR|-läˌ}})
* {{audio|en|en-us-mother-in-law.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|mothers-in-law|mother-in-laws|pl2qual=colloquial, nonstandard}}

# The [[mother#Noun|mother]] of one's [[spouse]].
